  "short_name": null,
  "language": "en",
  "description": "The Leeds Dependence Questionnaire (LDQ) is a brief, 10-item, self-report measure of substance dependence intended to capture the essential elements of the dependence syndrome across all substance classes. The LDQ can provide clinicians and researchers with a unitary, continuous, measure of dependence that is not specific to any particular substance (Edwards & Gross, 1976; Edwards, 1986).",
